# EnvironmentPostProcessors - each must run before any bean is created, in
# every entry point (main(), mvn spring-boot:run, @SpringBootTest); see each
# class's javadoc. EnvironmentPostProcessor is the only extension point that's
# actually guaranteed to fire that early, regardless of which of those three
# ways SpringApplication.run() got called.
#   - TimeZoneEnvironmentPostProcessor: pins JVM timezone before DataSource/Flyway.
#   - McpWindowsCommandEnvironmentPostProcessor: defaults MCP_*_COMMAND to
#     npx.cmd on Windows so application-mcp.yml's static stdio servers spawn
#     (npx vs npx.cmd / CreateProcess error=2) before McpClientAutoConfiguration
#     reads those commands.
#   - AuthModeEnvironmentPostProcessor: a blank or padded app.auth.mode means what an unset
#     one means (keycloak), so @ConditionalOnProperty on the mode behaves the same as the default.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.agenticai.core.TimeZoneEnvironmentPostProcessor,\
com.agenticai.core.McpWindowsCommandEnvironmentPostProcessor,\
com.agenticai.core.MigrateOnlyEnvironmentPostProcessor,\
com.agenticai.core.startup.StartupWarmupEnvironmentPostProcessor,\
com.agenticai.core.AuthModeEnvironmentPostProcessor

# Cold-start lane (2026-10-04), both inert unless app.startup.profiling.enabled=true:
#   - StartupProfilingInitializer installs Spring's BufferingApplicationStartup before the context refreshes.
#   - StartupProfilingReporter logs the slowest start-up steps (and optionally dumps the timeline JSON) at readiness.
org.springframework.context.ApplicationContextInitializer=\
com.agenticai.core.startup.StartupProfilingInitializer
org.springframework.context.ApplicationListener=\
com.agenticai.core.startup.StartupProfilingReporter
